WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:10.320
Evidence-based practice combines research with clinical expertise and the patient's values and circumstances. None of these inputs works well in isolation.
循证实践把研究证据、临床经验与患者的价值取向及处境结合起来，任何一项单独使用都不充分。

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:23.256
A study may describe an average benefit, but your patient may have different risks, resources or priorities. Clinical judgement asks whether the evidence fits this person and the care you are authorized to provide.
研究可能描述平均获益，但眼前患者的风险、资源或优先事项可能不同。临床判断需要确认：证据是否适用于这个人，以及自己获准提供的照护。

00:00:23.256 --> 00:00:33.456
Your experience helps you recognize patterns and implementation problems. It does not make a memorable success stronger than a well-conducted body of research.
经验有助于识别模式和实施困难，但一次印象深刻的成功，并不会因此比一整套严谨研究更有说服力。

00:00:33.456 --> 00:00:45.984
Likewise, a patient's preference matters even when it differs from the option with the best average result. Explain the options, check understanding and work within the applicable clinical guidance.
同样，即使患者偏好与平均结果最好的选择不同，其偏好仍然重要。应解释选项、核实理解，并在适用临床指导内开展照护。

00:00:45.984 --> 00:00:56.208
Quantitative research uses measured data. A trial comparing the frequency of missed handover information between two methods asks a quantitative question.
定量研究使用测量数据。试验比较两种交接方法遗漏信息的频率，提出的就是定量问题。

00:00:56.208 --> 00:01:08.856
Qualitative research explores experiences and meanings, often through interviews or observations. Asking why patients feel excluded during handover is a different and equally useful question.
定性研究常通过访谈或观察，探讨体验及其意义。询问患者为何在交接时感到被排除，是另一类同样有价值的问题。

00:01:08.856 --> 00:01:23.688
A randomized trial can reduce confounding for an intervention comparison. A cohort study follows groups without assigning treatment. A case report can reveal a problem but cannot reliably establish how often a treatment works.
随机试验能够减少干预比较中的混杂；队列研究观察人群而不分配治疗；个案报告可能揭示问题，却不能可靠确定治疗有效的频率。

00:01:23.688 --> 00:01:35.640
A systematic review brings studies together using explicit methods. Its value still depends on the included studies and how the review was performed, not simply its place on a hierarchy.
系统综述使用明确方法汇集研究，但其价值仍取决于纳入研究的质量及综述方法，而不是仅凭它在证据层级中的位置。

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:46.560
Knowledge translation connects research with actual practice. Findings need appraisal, synthesis and interpretation before they become a safe local process.
知识转化把研究连接到实际工作。研究发现需要经过评价、综合和解释，才能成为安全的本地流程。

00:01:46.560 --> 00:02:00.840
Prehospital care has particular constraints: moving vehicles, limited personnel, variable equipment and long distances to definitive care. Results from a well-resourced hospital may not transfer directly.
院前照护有特殊限制：行驶车辆、人员有限、设备差异，以及距离确定性治疗较远。资源充足的医院研究结果未必能直接移植。

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:12.480
Implementation includes the authorized protocol, team training, equipment and monitoring for unintended effects. An article does not itself add a procedure to your scope.
实施包括获授权的规程、团队培训、设备，以及监测非预期影响。论文本身不会把某项操作加入你的执业权限。

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:25.008
Report field barriers and audit results through the appropriate channel. Good feedback explains where a process failed and what resources were missing, rather than silently creating a private protocol.
通过适当渠道报告现场障碍和审核结果。有效反馈应说明流程在哪里失效、缺少什么资源，而不是私下默默创造自己的规程。

00:02:25.008 --> 00:02:35.928
PICO stands for population, intervention, comparison and outcome. It turns a broad question such as are prompts useful into a question that a study can answer.
PICO 分别指研究人群、干预、对照和结局。它把“提示卡是否有用”之类宽泛问题，转化为研究能够回答的问题。

00:02:35.928 --> 00:02:46.392
Our original example asks whether new paramedic students using a structured handover prompt omit less critical information than students using their usual approach.
我们的原创例子询问：新入学的院前急救学生使用结构化交接提示，是否比采用原有方法的学生遗漏更少关键信息。

00:02:46.392 --> 00:02:59.328
Specify outcomes before interpreting results. Fewer omissions may be valuable, but a delay in urgent treatment would also matter. A single convenient score may miss an important harm.
解释结果前先明确结局。遗漏减少可能有价值，但若延误紧急治疗，同样重要。单一、方便测量的评分可能漏掉重要损害。

00:02:59.328 --> 00:03:09.768
When reading an abstract, write these four elements in your own words. If the population or comparison is unclear, that uncertainty belongs in the appraisal.
阅读摘要时，用自己的话写出这四部分。如果研究人群或对照不清楚，这种不确定性应进入评价。

00:03:09.768 --> 00:03:19.656
Validity asks whether the estimate is trustworthy. Selection bias can occur when the people included differ systematically from those who should have been studied.
有效性关注估计是否可信。如果纳入者与本应研究的人群存在系统性差异，就可能产生选择偏倚。

00:03:19.656 --> 00:03:31.272
Confounding occurs when another difference between groups helps explain the outcome. If only experienced crews receive a new tool, experience may partly explain a better result.
混杂是指组间另一种差异有助于解释结局。例如只有资深团队获得新工具，结果更好就可能部分源自经验差异。

00:03:31.272 --> 00:03:42.456
Blinding can reduce influence from knowing the assigned intervention. In a simulation study, a student may see the prompt, while an assessor can still be blinded to the study group.
盲法能减少因知道干预分配而产生的影响。在模拟研究中，学生能看见提示卡，但评估员仍可能不知道其研究分组。

00:03:42.456 --> 00:03:54.336
Relevance is a separate judgement. A rigorously conducted classroom study can still leave uncertainty about noisy emergency scenes, experienced crews and actual patient outcomes.
适用性是另一项判断。即使课堂研究非常严谨，对于嘈杂急救现场、资深团队和真实患者结局，仍可能存在不确定性。

00:03:54.336 --> 00:04:04.440
An effect estimate describes the size of a difference. Its uncertainty matters: a small study may leave a wide range of plausible effects.
效应估计描述差异有多大；其不确定性也重要。小研究可能留下很宽的可能效应范围。

00:04:04.440 --> 00:04:18.024
A p-value is calculated under a specified statistical model, often a no-difference model. It concerns obtaining results at least as extreme as those observed, assuming that model and its assumptions.
p 值是在指定统计模型下计算的，通常采用“无差异”模型。在模型及其假设成立的前提下，它涉及出现至少与观察结果同样极端结果的概率。

00:04:18.024 --> 00:04:27.768
It is not the probability that the treatment works, or that the result was caused by chance. A threshold alone cannot establish clinical importance.
它不是治疗有效的概率，也不是结果由偶然造成的概率。仅凭一个阈值，不能确定临床重要性。

00:04:27.768 --> 00:04:39.648
Likewise, a result that is not statistically significant does not prove that two approaches are equivalent. Look at design, effect estimates and uncertainty before drawing a conclusion.
同样，没有统计学显著差异，并不证明两种方法等效。形成结论前，应同时查看设计、效应估计及不确定性。

00:04:39.648 --> 00:04:51.240
These numbers are invented solely for appraisal practice; they are not a published trial or evidence of clinical benefit. Thirty students in each group perform one simulated handover.
这些数字只为证据评价练习而虚构，不是已发表试验，也不是临床获益证据。每组三十名学生各完成一次模拟交接。

00:04:51.240 --> 00:05:02.280
The prompt group has fewer mean omissions but takes longer. Random allocation and a blinded assessor strengthen the design, provided they were actually implemented as described.
提示组平均遗漏较少，但花费时间更长。如果确实按描述实施，随机分配和评估员盲法会增强设计可信度。

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:12.888
Important questions remain: how was the checklist chosen, were groups comparable, were any students excluded, and how uncertain is the estimated difference?
仍有重要问题：核对表如何确定、两组是否可比、有无学生被排除，以及差异估计有多大不确定性？

00:05:12.888 --> 00:05:22.800
Write a conclusion that acknowledges both the possible benefit and the limits. Do not turn a classroom omission score into a claim that patient survival improves.
请写出同时承认潜在益处和局限的结论。不能把课堂遗漏评分直接改写为提高患者生存率。

00:05:22.800 --> 00:05:33.552
A cautious but useful conclusion is: the prompt may reduce omissions in this student simulation, but the estimate is incomplete and the longer handover needs attention.
谨慎而有用的结论可以是：提示卡可能减少本次学生模拟中的遗漏，但估计信息不完整，交接时间延长也值得关注。

00:05:33.552 --> 00:05:45.096
Ask for the full methods and uncertainty estimates before judging strength. The study does not tell us whether the result persists, generalizes to the field or benefits patients.
判断证据强度前，应索取完整方法和不确定性估计。研究没有说明效果是否持久、能否推广到现场，或是否使患者获益。

00:05:45.096 --> 00:05:57.288
For an educational improvement, a supervised pilot might be reasonable after approval. Define what would count as a successful change and watch for delays or mechanical checklist reading.
对于教学改进，获准后开展受督导试点可能合理。事先界定何谓成功，并留意延误或机械照读清单的问题。

00:05:57.288 --> 00:06:09.624
For a clinical intervention, evidence review must also pass through the appropriate governance, scope, training and protocol process. Personal enthusiasm is not implementation authority.
对于临床干预，证据审查还必须进入适当管理、权限、培训和规程流程。个人热情不等于实施授权。

00:06:09.624 --> 00:06:21.000
AET asks you to think about PARAMEDIC2. This randomized, double-blind UK trial compared epinephrine with saline placebo during adult out-of-hospital cardiac arrest.
AET 要求思考 PARAMEDIC2。这项英国随机双盲试验，在成人院外心脏骤停中比较肾上腺素与生理盐水安慰剂。

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:35.952
Thirty-day survival was 3.2 percent versus 2.4 percent. Favourable neurological outcome at discharge was 2.2 percent versus 1.9 percent, without a statistically significant difference.
三十天生存率分别为百分之三点二和百分之二点四；出院时良好神经功能结局分别为百分之二点二和百分之一点九，未发现统计学显著差异。

00:06:35.952 --> 00:07:01.488
At discharge, severe neurological impairment was reported in thirty-nine of one hundred and twenty-six survivors given epinephrine, versus sixteen of ninety placebo survivors. Those are survivor denominators, not all randomized patients. Discuss this finding alongside the separate survival and favourable-outcome comparisons; it does not establish what caused every survivor's disability.
出院时，肾上腺素组一百二十六名幸存者中三十九人、安慰剂组九十名幸存者中十六人被报告有严重神经功能障碍。分母是幸存者，不是所有随机分配者。须结合独立的生存和良好结局比较讨论，不能据此确定每位幸存者障碍的原因。

00:07:01.488 --> 00:07:12.384
Appraisal is also different from issuing a treatment order. Use the applicable resuscitation protocol and your authorization; this lesson does not change either.
评价研究也不同于发布治疗指令。实际照护应使用适用的复苏规程和本人权限；本课不改变任何一项。

00:07:12.384 --> 00:07:21.960
A practice gap is a difference between your current performance and an appropriate standard. It is a starting point for learning, not a verdict about your worth.
实践差距是当前表现与适当标准之间的差异。它是学习的起点，不是对个人价值的判决。

00:07:21.960 --> 00:07:32.904
Internal triggers include hesitation or uncertainty. External triggers include a preceptor's feedback, a documentation audit, a near miss or a changed guideline.
内部触发因素包括犹豫和不确定；外部触发因素包括带教反馈、记录审核、未遂事件或指南更新。

00:07:32.904 --> 00:07:45.024
Describe the behaviour, its context and its consequence. I omitted treatment response in two simulated handovers is actionable; I am bad at communication is too broad.
描述具体行为、情境和后果。“两次模拟交接漏报治疗反应”可以指导行动；“我不擅长沟通”则过于宽泛。

00:07:45.024 --> 00:08:07.320
Compare your impression with observed feedback. The school uses the Dunning-Kruger label to highlight that limited skill can also limit recognition of mistakes. Treat it as a reason to seek calibration, not a diagnosis of every confident novice. Confidence can rise without skill improving; an uncertain student may still perform accurately.
把自我印象与实际观察反馈相比较。学校用Dunning-Kruger标签提醒：技能有限，也可能限制识别自身错误的能力。应把它作为寻求校准反馈的理由，不是给每个自信新手的诊断。信心可能增加而技能未改善；不自信的学生也可能表现准确。

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:17.856
SWOT separates internal strengths and weaknesses from external opportunities and threats. It helps you plan around real conditions instead of listing vague ambitions.
SWOT 把内部优势和不足，与外部机会和威胁分开，帮助你依据真实条件计划，而不是罗列模糊愿望。

00:08:17.856 --> 00:08:29.904
A strength could be a consistent assessment sequence. A weakness could be missing the latest observations during handover. An opportunity could be access to a supervised simulation lab.
优势可以是评估顺序稳定；不足可以是交接时漏报最新观察；机会可以是能够使用受督导的模拟实验室。

00:08:29.904 --> 00:08:41.088
A threat might be a shift pattern that prevents attendance at one lab. Change the action plan by arranging another supervised session, rather than lowering the safety standard.
威胁可能是班次安排使你无法参加某次实验课。应调整行动安排，例如另约督导练习，而不是降低安全标准。

00:08:41.088 --> 00:08:52.128
The downloaded AET teaching asks for at least two weaknesses and at least one opportunity in the personal CPD document. Use genuine observations from your own learning.
已下载的 AET 教学要求在个人 CPD 文件中列出至少两项不足及至少一个机会。应使用自己学习过程中的真实观察。

00:08:52.128 --> 00:09:01.248
DACA means describe, analyze, conclude and act. Start with a brief factual account, not an exhaustive retelling of the call.
DACA 指描述、分析、结论和行动。先用简短事实概括，而不是事无巨细地重述整次出车。

00:09:01.248 --> 00:09:15.120
In our fictional simulation, the student reported the first blood pressure but omitted the newer reading. Analysis asks why: perhaps the note layout hid the trend and rehearsal focused only on the initial assessment.
在我们的虚构模拟中，学生报告了首次血压，却漏报较新的读数。分析应追问原因，例如笔记版式掩盖趋势，或排练只关注初次评估。

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:26.352
The conclusion is a specific learning need: communicating the latest status and meaningful change. The action should practise that exact behaviour and include independent feedback.
结论是具体学习需要：表达最新状态及重要变化。行动应练习这一行为，并包含独立反馈。

00:09:26.352 --> 00:09:38.352
Keep identifiable patient details out of a personal learning portfolio. Reflection needs enough context to explain the learning, not enough detail to reconstruct a patient's identity.
个人学习档案不要包含可识别患者的细节。反思需要足够背景解释学习点，而不是足够细节还原患者身份。

00:09:38.352 --> 00:09:50.544
SMART stands for specific, measurable, achievable, relevant and time-bound. A goal states the improvement you want to demonstrate; an activity is how you plan to reach it.
SMART 指具体、可衡量、可实现、相关和有时限。目标描述想证明的改进；活动则是达到目标的方式。

00:09:50.544 --> 00:10:04.248
Read about handover is an activity, not a performance outcome. A better goal is to deliver three varied simulated handovers with the latest observations, trends and treatment response, checked by a supervisor.
“阅读交接资料”是活动，不是表现结果。更好的目标是完成三个不同的模拟交接，报告最新观察、趋势及治疗反应，并由督导核查。

00:10:04.248 --> 00:10:15.384
Set a feasible date and a clear success criterion. The practice count is an example for your plan, not an AET pass mark or proof of independent clinical competence.
设定可行日期和清晰成功标准。这里的练习次数是计划示例，不是 AET 合格分数，也不能证明具备独立临床能力。

00:10:15.384 --> 00:10:27.336
If the goal depends on rare real patient opportunities, choose a supervised simulation alternative. Do not perform an unnecessary procedure merely to complete a learning target.
如果目标依赖罕见真实患者机会，应选择受督导模拟作为替代。不能只为完成学习目标而实施不必要操作。

00:10:27.336 --> 00:10:36.792
A CPD plan connects a gap to a goal, actions, evidence, dates and review. Each part should support the same learning need.
CPD 计划把差距连接到目标、行动、证据、日期和复核。每一部分都应支持同一个学习需要。

00:10:36.792 --> 00:10:48.984
Select a resource because it addresses the gap. For a local handover process, the applicable service guideline is more directly relevant than a general article about communication.
根据是否能解决差距选择资料。针对本地交接流程，适用机构指南通常比一篇泛泛讨论沟通的文章更直接相关。

00:10:48.984 --> 00:10:58.920
Plan both learning and performance. Reading explains the framework; rehearsal and observed feedback show whether you can use it under realistic conditions.
计划既要包含知识学习，也要包含表现练习。阅读用于理解框架；排练和观察反馈用于检验能否在接近真实的条件下使用。

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:09.792
Document a review date before starting. If the result is not achieved, change the learning action or obtain further support, and record the remaining gap honestly.
开始前就记录复核日期。如果未达到结果，应调整学习行动或取得进一步支持，并如实记录仍存在的差距。

00:11:09.792 --> 00:11:21.144
This is an original example, not a completed answer to the school's capstone. The performance gap is omission of a clinically important change, not simply a lack of confidence.
这是原创示例，不是学校综合作业的完成答案。表现差距是漏报重要临床变化，而不只是信心不足。

00:11:21.144 --> 00:11:32.736
The learner reviews the applicable handover guideline, changes the note layout to show times and trends, and practises three different scenarios with a supervisor before the next skills session.
学习者阅读适用交接指南，调整笔记版式以显示时间和趋势，并在下一次技能课前，由督导观察练习三个不同场景。

00:11:32.736 --> 00:11:44.496
The supervisor records whether the latest findings, major change and treatment response were communicated. The learner keeps a de-identified checklist and a short DACA reflection.
督导记录是否传达了最新结果、主要变化和治疗反应。学习者保留去标识的核对表和简短 DACA 反思。

00:11:44.496 --> 00:11:54.576
A later repeat checks retention. If the learner still reads only the first measurements, the gap remains open even though the reading and practice sessions were completed.
稍后再次练习以检查保持效果。如果学习者仍只读出首次测量，即使已完成阅读和练习，差距仍未解决。

00:11:54.576 --> 00:12:10.968
Formal activities include structured courses and workshops. Informal development can include self-directed reading, peer discussion and reflection. Both can support learning, but credit eligibility depends on the applicable regulatory rules.
正式活动包括结构化课程和工作坊；非正式发展可包括自主阅读、同伴讨论和反思。两者都能支持学习，但能否计入学分，取决于适用监管规则。

00:12:10.968 --> 00:12:33.408
The school's six-part reflective entry asks what happened, what you learned, why it matters, what action you took, what evidence you kept and when you will review it. Add the activity and date, organize by topic and retain the supporting record. Separate a planned action from a completed one; a tidy folder does not itself prove improvement.
学校六部分反思条目要求写明：发生什么、学到什么、为何重要、采取什么行动、保留什么证据，以及何时复核。应补充活动及日期，按主题组织并保留支持材料。须区分计划与已完成行动；整齐文件夹本身不证明改进。

00:12:33.408 --> 00:12:46.008
A personal portfolio is not a copy of the patient chart. Remove direct identifiers and combinations that could identify a person, especially in a small community or an unusual event.
个人档案不是患者病历副本。移除直接身份信息，以及可能识别个人的细节组合，尤其是小社区或罕见事件中的组合。

00:12:46.008 --> 00:12:54.960
Use approved secure systems for any official patient-contact reporting. A private teaching example should contain no identifiable clinical record.
正式患者接触报告应使用获准的安全系统。个人教学示例不应包含可识别的临床记录。

00:12:54.960 --> 00:13:05.616
A weak entry records only attendance. A stronger entry explains the learning need, the learning itself and how it influenced a decision or performance.
薄弱记录只证明参加过活动；更有力的记录解释学习需要、具体学到什么，以及怎样影响决定或表现。

00:13:05.616 --> 00:13:18.024
For example: I learned to pair each intervention with a timed response; my supervisor observed that all three rehearsed handovers included this information; I will repeat the task next week.
例如：“我学会把每项干预与带时间的反应配对；督导观察到三次排练均包含该信息；我将在下周再次检查。”

00:13:18.024 --> 00:13:29.112
Keep the actual evidence where permitted. Do not claim an audit proved improvement if no comparison was made, and do not write a planned action as though it has already occurred.
在规则允许范围内保留真实证据。没有进行比较，就不能声称审核已证明改进；计划中的行动，也不能写成已经发生。

00:13:29.112 --> 00:13:39.024
A useful portfolio can show an unfinished gap honestly. That makes it possible to obtain further learning rather than disguising attendance as mastery.
有用的档案可以如实显示尚未解决的差距。这样才能取得进一步学习，而不是把出席伪装成掌握。

00:13:39.024 --> 00:13:48.912
Review a CPD plan after meaningful feedback and at scheduled intervals. Successful practice may close one gap while revealing another.
得到重要反馈后，以及到预定时间时，都应复核 CPD 计划。成功练习可能解决一个差距，同时暴露另一个。

00:13:48.912 --> 00:14:00.960
Keep school completion, service training and regulatory continuing competence distinct. One activity may support more than one purpose, but automatic credit should not be assumed.
把学校课程完成、机构培训和监管持续胜任要求区分开。一项活动可能支持多个目的，但不能假定会自动获得相应学分。

00:14:00.960 --> 00:14:14.448
The current BC regulation describes continuing education, patient contacts, reporting and supporting records, with defined exceptions. Check the requirements applicable to your licence and reporting period.
现行卑诗省法规规定继续教育、患者接触、报告及支持记录，同时设有明确例外。应核实自己执照和报告期适用的要求。

00:14:14.448 --> 00:14:27.408
For this week, the immediate learning task is a specific, defensible personal development plan. A well-organized portfolio supports that task, but organization alone does not prove clinical competence.
本周眼前的学习任务是形成具体、可辩护的个人发展计划。组织良好的档案有助于完成任务，但整齐的档案本身不能证明临床胜任能力。

00:14:27.408 --> 00:14:37.728
The downloaded teaching asks you to build a personal CPD document and complete a capstone using a school-provided vignette and template. Your work must be your own.
已下载教学要求建立个人 CPD 文件，并使用学校提供的情境和模板完成综合任务。作业应由你本人完成。

00:14:37.728 --> 00:15:02.040
The saved instructions require at least one SMART, patient-centred goal and at least one relevant evidence source that you appraise and justify. The criteria connect a specific learning need, a measurable improvement action, evidence-based relevance and complete documentation. Explain those connections using your own work, not an invented completed experience.
保存的说明要求至少一个以患者为中心的SMART目标，以及至少一项经过评价并说明理由的相关证据来源。标准把具体学习需要、可衡量改进行动、循证相关性及记录完整性相连。应以本人工作解释这些联系，不能编造已经完成的经历。

00:15:02.040 --> 00:15:11.616
A blank planning aid is included with this lecture. It is not the official school template, a submitted assignment or a model answer to the school's vignette.
本课附带空白规划辅助表。它不是学校官方模板，不是已提交作业，也不是学校情境的示范答案。

00:15:11.616 --> 00:15:21.648
Before submission, confirm the current school instructions and form. This course does not open assessments, submit work or mark an LMS task complete.
提交前核实当前学校说明和表格。本课程不会打开考核、代交作业，或把 LMS 任务标记为完成。
